==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbɪkə/}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪkə(r)}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm}} {{term|bikeren|lang=enm}} 'to attack', from {{etyl|dum}} {{term|bicken|lang=nl}} 'to stab, attack' (modern {{term|bikken|lang=nl}} 'to chip off'), from {{proto|Germanic|bikjanan}} (compare Old English {{term|becca|lang=ang}} 'pickax', Old High German {{term|bicchan|lang=goh}} 'to thrust, attack', Old Norse {{term|bikkja|lang=non}} 'to plunge into water'); of unknown origin.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[quarrel]] in a [[tiresome]], insulting manner.
#: ''They '''bickered''' about dinner every evening.''

====Synonyms====
* [[wrangle]]
* See also [[Wikisaurus:squabble]]

